<title>BRAZIL: Sao Paulo Jan unemployment 13.9 pct -- Dieese.</title>
<headline>Sao Paulo Jan unemployment 13.9 pct -- Dieese.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The unemployment rate in Sao Paulo city rose to 13.9 percent in January, up from 13.1 percent in the same month 1996, the Labor Union Statistics Institute (Dieese) reported.</p>
<p>The number of unemployed workers rose to 1.173 million in January, up from 1.076 million in January last year, it said.</p>
<p>January figures, however, dropped against December 1996 when the share of unemployed workers hit 14.2 percent of the workforce, or 1.208 million workers, it added.</p>
<p>((-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5415))</p>
